{"repositoryId":890987854,"availability":"available","full":"with-ours/ours-nextjs-example","name":"ours-nextjs-example","description":"This repository provides a working example of integrating the Ours analytics platform with a Next.js application. It demonstrates how to set up the Ours tracking script, track page views, and log custom events like button clicks or form submissions—all while maintaining privacy and HIPAA compliance.","category":"Other","language":"TypeScript","stars":1,"forks":0,"created":"2024-11-19T14:32:09Z","updated":"2026-10-12T21:29:30Z","branch":"main","homepage":null,"topics":[],"demo":"https://docs.oursprivacy.com/","color":"#323057","ink":"#d6caff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-13T07:38:05.027Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-13T07:38:05.027Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-13T07:38:05.027Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-13T07:38:05.027Z","stars":1,"forks":0}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["This repo is a working reference for integrating the Ours Privacy CDP (Customer Data Platform) and CMP (Consent Management Platform) into a Next.js application. Browse the code to see how each product is installed, initialized, and used.","In Next.js, a layout is a component that wraps every page in its directory. Layouts are the right place to load analytics and consent scripts because:","This project has four product-specific nested layouts:"],"features":["They run once — the layout mounts when a visitor enters that section of your site. Scripts initialize once and persist across page navigations.","They wrap all child pages — every page inside the layout folder automatically gets the scripts without repeating code.","They compose — the root layout provides global things (nav, fonts, CSS), and nested layouts add product-specific scripts on top."],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/with-ours/ours-nextjs-example/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"8ca70fd56db350d483d37ea7fd7396f9b3f58f5234480e399a836b679f692c0c","extractedAt":"2026-1